    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d83">

                <pb facs="0123" n="109" xml:id="pg109"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">501.BC
                    Indonesia/3–148: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Consulate General at Batavia
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">us urgent</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-03-01">March 1, 1948</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>85. Usgoc 71. Following resolutions proposed by
                    Canada (Document S/678) and China (Document S/P.V. 259) respectively, were
                    adopted by SC at its 259th meeting, 28 Feb
                        1948:<anchor n="1" xml:id="d83-f1"/>
                </p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item> “<hi rendition="#small-caps">The Security Council</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#small-caps">having</hi> considered the Report of the
                            Committee of Good Offices, informing the Council of the steps taken by
                            the Netherlands Government and the Government of the Republic of
                            Indonesia to comply with the Council’s resolution of 1 August
                            1947;</item>
                        <label/>
                        <item>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Notes</hi> with satisfaction the signing of
                            the Truce Agreement by both parties and the acceptance by both parties
                            of certain principles as an agreed basis for the conclusion of a
                            political settlement in Indonesia;</item>
                        <label/>
                        <item>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Commends</hi> the members of the Committee
                            of Good Offices for the assistance they have given the two parties in
                            their endeavours to settle their dispute by peaceful means;</item>
                        <label/>
                        <item>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Maintains</hi> its offer of good offices
                            contained in the resolution of 25 August 1947, and, to this end,</item>
                        <label/>
                        <item>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Requests</hi> both parties and the Committee
                            of Good Offices to keep the Council directly informed about the progress
                            of the political settlement in Indonesia.”</item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>“The Security Council requests the Committee of Good Offices to pay
                            particular attention to the political development in Western Java and
                            Madura and to report to the Council thereon at frequent
                            intervals.”</item>
                    </list>
                </quote>
                <p>(Repeated to The Hague as 75).</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
